# CMS (Sanity Studio)

## Config

- Studio v6 in `cms/` — `sanity.config.js`, schemas in `cms/schemaTypes/`
- Project: `sfqhf74q`, dataset: `production`
- Commands: `npm run dev` (studio), `npm run deploy` (hosted studio)

## Schema design

Model content to match frontend shapes in `frontend/src/mockData.js` and `frontend/src/data/`:

- **product** — name, slug, price, origin, abv, style, category ref, type, description, images (card + gallery)
- **category** — key/slug, title, description (maps to `CATEGORIES`)
- **article** — knowledge posts (`/kien-thuc/[slug]`)
- **policy** — legal pages (`/chinh-sach/[slug]`)
- **banner** — hero carousel slides

Use `defineType` / `defineField`. Slugs via Sanity slug field; keep ASCII slugs consistent with frontend routes.

## Rules

- Let Sanity generate `_id` for ordinary documents; use explicit IDs only for singletons
- Model relationships with `reference` fields + GROQ lookups
- Add validation (required fields, slug format, image alt text)
- Prettier config: single quotes, no semis, printWidth 100

## Frontend integration

Sanity content is fetched **server-side at runtime** on Cloudflare Workers:

- Client: `frontend/src/lib/sanity/client.js`
- Data store: `frontend/src/lib/sanity/productStore.js`
- Env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET`
- Pages use `export const revalidate = 60` for ISR-like caching
- Falls back to `mockData.js` when Sanity is empty or unreachable

See project skill `luvinico-sanity-cms` for GROQ and schema details.
